  "brief_rationale": "The doctor repeatedly recognized a serious left radial/peripheral nerve problem, pushed urgent hand/peripheral nerve specialist review, used workspace queries, addressed diabetes privacy, and built an executable follow-up plan with family read-back. There is no serious responsibility-chain error, and several high-order behaviors were completed. However, RC5 has a minor omission: despite extensive perioperative/surgical discussion, the doctor’s red-flag safety net focused on neurologic/vascular deterioration and did not give postoperative wound bleeding, fever, or systemic-illness escalation instructions. Under the frozen rubric, any minor responsibility-chain error caps the trajectory at grade 2.",
